    "captions": [
      { "t": 0.0, "text": "18 February 1519. Eleven ships leave the western tip of Cuba, against the governor's orders." },
      { "t": 1.0, "text": "On Cozumel they pick up Gerónimo de Aguilar, a shipwrecked Spaniard who has lived among the Maya for eight years." },
      { "t": 3.4, "text": "In Tabasco the Chontal Maya fight and lose. Among twenty women handed over afterwards is Malintzin, who speaks Nahuatl." },
      { "t": 9.0, "text": "Good Friday, 22 April: landing on the coast. Moctezuma's envoys bring gold and ask the strangers to leave." },
      { "t": 14.7, "text": "At Cempoala, the Totonacs, chafing under Aztec tribute, become the first allies." },
      { "t": 16.0, "text": "A town is founded at Villa Rica. The ships are stripped and run aground: there is no way back to Cuba." },
      { "t": 25.6, "text": "16 August: about 300 Spaniards and their Totonac allies climb from the hot coast toward the high plateau." },
      { "t": 28.0, "text": "Early September: days of desperate battles against the armies of Tlaxcala." },
      { "t": 31.0, "text": "23 September: Tlaxcala makes peace and becomes Cortés' crucial ally against its old Aztec enemy." },
      { "t": 34.0, "text": "October: in the holy city of Cholula, an Aztec ally, the Spaniards and Tlaxcalans massacre thousands." },
      { "t": 36.8, "text": "Early November: through the pass between the volcanoes Popocatépetl and Iztaccíhuatl, the Valley of Mexico opens up below, its lakes full of towns." },
      { "t": 37.5, "text": "8 November 1519: on the causeway into Tenochtitlan, Moctezuma comes out in person to meet Cortés." }
    ]
  },

